*.o
# Anchored.  Unanchored it matched client/assets/ui/table.png as well,
# because this filesystem does not care about case -- which is how the
# table texture stayed out of a repository that was meant to carry it.
/TABLE.png
# art/ is NOT ignored.  It is the one generated thing that cannot be
# generated again: gen-art.py queues every face with seed -1 and
# logs/jobs.tsv records only the job id, so re-running the same prompts
# yields 1455 different pictures.  The backs ARE reproducible --
# BACKS.tsv keeps model, seed and prompt for each.  art/ is kept
# because the faces are composed from it whenever a card's text
# changes, not because the game reads it.
/card-*.png
client/.godot/
# The faces, the backs, the UI surfaces and the card list are all in
# the repository now.  They are generated, and the old rule was that
# generated things are regenerated -- but the rule that matters is that
# somebody who clones this can run it.  Composing 1455 faces is a few
# minutes and needs ImageMagick; a clone should not need either.
#
# The small faces are the one exception: _card_tex falls back to the
# full face when a thumb is missing, so they cost 231MB and change
# nothing a player can see.  make setup makes them.
client/assets/thumbs/
court
logs/
/sheet*.png
__pycache__/
client/backgrounds/
